<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>ROS2 on Ricardo</title><link>https://Ricardo-Guo.github.io/tags/ros2/</link><description>Recent content in ROS2 on Ricardo</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><copyright>Ricardo</copyright><lastBuildDate>Wed, 24 Apr 2024 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://Ricardo-Guo.github.io/tags/ros2/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>OpenVINS-based UAV Swarm Cooperative Self-Localization System</title><link>https://Ricardo-Guo.github.io/projects/openvins-uav-swarm/</link><pubDate>Wed, 24 Apr 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://Ricardo-Guo.github.io/projects/openvins-uav-swarm/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://Ricardo-Guo.github.io/projects/openvins-uav-swarm/openvins-cover.svg" alt="Featured image of post OpenVINS-based UAV Swarm Cooperative Self-Localization System" />&lt;h2 id="-project-overview">🎯 Project Overview
&lt;/h2>&lt;p>&lt;strong>Solving the drift problem in UAV swarm operations without GPS dependency.&lt;/strong>&lt;/p>
&lt;p>This project implements a comprehensive visual-inertial odometry (VIO) system for UAV swarms, combining &lt;strong>OpenVINS&lt;/strong>, &lt;strong>ROS2 communication architecture&lt;/strong>, and &lt;strong>cooperative localization algorithms&lt;/strong> to achieve high-precision positioning in both simulation and real-world environments.&lt;/p>
&lt;h3 id="tech-stack">Tech Stack
&lt;/h3>&lt;ul>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Middleware&lt;/strong>: ROS2 (Humble)&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Programming&lt;/strong>: C++17, Python&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>VIO Engine&lt;/strong>: OpenVINS&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Simulation&lt;/strong>: Gazebo Sim(Fortress), PX4 SITL&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Flight Control&lt;/strong>: PX4 Autopilot, MAVROS&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Computer Vision&lt;/strong>: OpenCV, Eigen&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Optimization&lt;/strong>: Ceres Solver, g2o&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Visualization&lt;/strong>: RViz2&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;hr>
&lt;h2 id="-simulation">🖥️ Simulation
&lt;/h2>&lt;h3 id="gazebo-physical-simulation">Gazebo Physical Simulation
&lt;/h3>&lt;p>We built a high-fidelity simulation environment with:&lt;/p>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Realistic lighting&lt;/strong> and shadow rendering&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Physically accurate&lt;/strong> UAV dynamics and sensor noise models&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Multi-UAV spawn system&lt;/strong> with collision avoidance&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;p>&lt;img src="https://Ricardo-Guo.github.io/gazebo_simulation.jpg"
loading="lazy"
alt="Gazebo Simulation Screenshot"
>
&lt;em>Figure: Multi-UAV cooperative exploration in a complex environment&lt;/em>&lt;/p>
&lt;h3 id="rviz2-visualization">RViz2 Visualization
&lt;/h3>&lt;p>Our visualization pipeline displays:&lt;/p>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Trajectory tracking&lt;/strong> (Path messages with color-coded time series)&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>3D Point Cloud Maps&lt;/strong> from stereo vision&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Real-time pose estimation&lt;/strong> with uncertainty ellipsoids&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;p>&lt;img src="https://Ricardo-Guo.github.io/rviz_visualization.jpg"
loading="lazy"
alt="RViz Visualization"
>
&lt;em>Figure: Real-time visualization of UAV poses, trajectories, and point cloud maps&lt;/em>&lt;/p>
&lt;h3 id="swarm-algorithm-visualization">Swarm Algorithm Visualization
&lt;/h3>&lt;p>&lt;strong>Distributed State Estimation Architecture:&lt;/strong>&lt;/p>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>Leader UAV runs independent OpenVINS node&lt;/li>
&lt;li>Follower UAVs receive leader&amp;rsquo;s pose estimate via ROS2 topic&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;p>&lt;img src="https://Ricardo-Guo.github.io/swarm_architecture.jpg"
loading="lazy"
alt="Swarm Visualization"
>
&lt;em>Figure: Distributed estimation with centralized optimization&lt;/em>&lt;/p>
